s the `b == 0` guard and uses `wrapping_rem`.\n\n## Verification (my own commands, not self-reports)\n1. **Symbol gate:** built the real CMake target (`libharvest-work-KPED2m.so`) and diffed `nm -D --defined-only` against the Rust `.so` → **identical, 11/11, empty diff**, with no extra Rust exports leaking (filtered check returned nothing for both).\n2. **Behaviour gate:** a `dlopen`-based differential harness (`.verify/diff_test.c`) loads both libraries side by side and compares **all 11 symbols** — including `memcmp` of the full 248-byte `ResultArray` after `init_result_array`/`process_with_foreach`/`compute_weighted_sum`, random `f64` bit patterns for `safe_double_to_int`, out-of-range/negative indices, counts 0–13 and negative, and `arrayfunc` over a dense grid + 500k random quadruples: **2,649,898 checks, 0 mismatches**.\n\n`cargo build --release` compiles clean with zero warnings; `c_src/` is untouched (still exactly 3 files, no build artifacts). Verification artifacts live in `.verify/`, outside the crate, so no stray `.so` sits in `translation/`. One deliberate skip in the harness: `INT_MIN % -1` hardware-traps (SIGFPE) in the compiled C, so it can't be compared — unreachable from `arrayfunc` since `rank` is always ≥ 0."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":428,"cache_read_input_tokens":45480,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":428,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07c2df7c-0eb0-4698-b7ff-581a8cb7bb09","uuid":"10d9d7a5-8a0c-40b1-8c6a-6ebfbb3b7b94","timestamp":"2026-08-27T21:51:55.748Z"}
